Dot notation for properties is not SSL (diag.dot_property_access, error,
on the .name fragment): after a variable, a call result and a subscript
(issue #255).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReadSubject;
	:DECLARE oMail, aRows, vOut;
	oMail := Email{};
	vOut := oMail.Subject;
	vOut := aRows[1].Name;
	vOut := Today().Year;
	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReadSubject;
	:DECLARE oMail, aRows, vOut;
	oMail := Email{};
	vOut := oMail.Subject;
	vOut := aRows[1].Name;
	vOut := Today().Year;
	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:15-4:23 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:Subject' instead of 'object.Subject'
5:18-5:23 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:Name' instead of 'object.Name'
6:17-6:22 error dot_property_access: SSL uses colon ':' for property access, not dot '.'. Use 'object:Year' instead of 'object.Year'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
